// (the whole wanted list: the worker opens the missing tabs and closes the ones no longer wanted; specs: the managed markets' decimals), tabs-exec {actions, specs}, tabs-close,
// tabs-status. SW -> leader page, no rid: follower-ready, follower-lost, follower-failed {accountId}. Follower page -> SW:
// follower-ready {accountId}, and follower-snap {accountId, snap} (the tab's own account, see below). SW -> follower page: exec {rid, actions},
// answered with {op:'reply', rid, results, snap}. The leader page also gets follower-snap from the worker (relayed as it came).
//
// The follower tab is the authority for its own account (round 4): the leader tab's store and REST view of a follower lagged by seconds in
// the owner's live test, and an acknowledged order that they did not show was sent again. The tab is pinned to the account, so its own store
// is live for it. It pushes {at, positions, orders, events} on every change of its account (at most 4 a second, CE_T.snapGapMs), as a heartbeat
// (CE_T.beatMs), with every exec answer and once more CE_T.afterMs after one (tagged with that exec's rid). 'events' are the REJECTED /
// CANCELLED / FILLED events of its orders. The leader reads a follower from it first (cpTabSnap / cpTabRead in 00-core.js).
//
// The follower tab (/trade/<market>?bvCopy=<accountId>) runs ONLY the copy executor at the bottom of this file: the suite itself stands
// down there (src/better-vest.user.js) and so does the Calendar (src/journal-page.js); the copier's widget, sub dock and test run are
